; Stage 15 W9 item 8's boundary: `as` narrows a literal only when the literal
; FITS. 300 does not fit i8, so this stays lossy and must be spelled
; `unsafe/cast` — the range test is `int-literal-fits`, the same predicate the
; implicit path is gated with, so the two accept exactly the same set.
;
; Compiling this must FAIL with:
;   "as: lossy conversion from i32 to i8 -- use unsafe/cast"
(defn main ():i32
  (let (a:i8 (as i8 300))
    (return (as i32 a))))
